# `*.txt' above is aimed at simulation output, but it also swallows every
# CMakeLists.txt -- a build file, not build output.  The existing ones (root,
# src/, python_src/, ...) are unaffected only because they were already tracked
# when the rule landed, and ignore rules never apply to tracked files.  Any
# CMakeLists.txt added to a NEW subdirectory since then has been invisible, and
# silently so: the build works locally and the file is simply missing from the
# clone.  That is how coupled_driver/ and tests/test-multi-membrane/ ended up
# untracked.
#
# Safe against build trees: `build/' is excluded as a DIRECTORY (line 12), and
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so generated
# CMakeLists.txt under a build tree stays ignored.
!CMakeLists.txt
